# Paired native controls: descriptive quality and custody review

Both fresh native controls score **165/200 (82.5%)** with the unchanged frozen strict scorer. Each has **191 natural stops and 9 length terminations**. The nine length cases receive no extracted answer and zero credit. Both controls answer the same 165 cases correctly; the remaining 35 comprise 26 naturally stopped wrong answers and nine truncations. No naturally stopped answer is invalid under the frozen extractor.

| Control | Process | Controller terminal UTC | Correct | Stop / length | Strict all_complete |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| native-quality-v2-hccl-true-01 | 287392 | 2026-10-25 23:55:07 | 165/200 | 191 / 9 | false |
| native-quality-v2-hccl-true-02 | 633998 | 2026-10-26 02:23:18 | 165/200 | 191 / 9 | false |

The common-correct set contains **165 cases** and the lower native correct-count floor is **165**. Both complete case lists and both per-case score tables are retained in [paired-description.json](paired-description.json). These are descriptions of the two native controls. **No candidate or supplementary acceptance gate was evaluated.** The original strict gate cannot pass its required native-completeness condition because each native control has nine length terminations; nothing here changes that rule or resolves Issue23.

For each control, the frozen exact binomial 95% interval is **76.512%–87.498%**. The frozen native2-versus-native1 paired comparison has 165 correct/correct, 35 wrong/wrong, and zero discordant cases; its conservative difference interval is **−2.167 to +2.167 percentage points**. These fixed-subset statistics do not establish population equivalence or arbitrary-text correctness.

The audit independently decoded every saved token array with the frozen tokenizer and verified all 200 output texts per control. Across controls, all 200 complete token arrays, texts and termination records are identical. Frozen plan, producer, gold/input files, prompt text/token digests, tokenizer bytes, exact source/environment/configuration, ordinary native worker, effective settings, and all 50 admission records per run passed their checks. Both use the recorded Ascend `BalanceScheduler`; no candidate worker was substituted. The frozen producer checks each returned prompt against the prescribed token IDs before retaining the output; this review verifies that producer and input binding, not model input tensors.

Both complete scheduler receipt files match their recorded SHA256. The unchanged receipt-binding helper validates admitted IDs, actual scheduled phases, D retirement and chronology. Each native run contains **95,857 transactions / 191,714 receipt rows**, with one observed native P-scheduled/D-retired transaction in each of the 25 batches and no preemption. Replacing only internal request IDs with their frozen case IDs makes the entire retained scheduler metadata identical: SHA256 `71c867f6a3730039f4523ce7925b9ca3b624008b328d9ace87a62449ee0c5de6`. Plugin-specific P-layer coverage is not a native-control requirement, and these metadata checks do not prove physical overlap.

Both terminal controllers have exit 0, complete collection, returned shutdown, empty recorded process tables for physical cards 1/2/3/6, and no timeout/forced-controller termination. A read-only `/proc` check found both recorded producer PIDs and live process-group members absent. **Both native logs retain SIGTERM fallback for four workers after the grace period**, so this is bounded cleanup evidence, not a globally graceful or signal-free shutdown claim.

The first control's earlier standalone description was reproduced exactly and left unchanged. Every reviewed input hash was checked unchanged after the audit. Full model weights were not rehashed: the frozen supplementary loader validated the existing full-weight manifest and unchanged size/mtime metadata. No frozen code, protocol, threshold, input or attempt was modified; no model/device/GitHub action was performed. The separate new N2 capsule is for a later publication batch and is excluded from fixed v4.
